{
  "_comment": [
    "The authd service definition: what peinit starts, and how.",
    "",
    "peinit used to carry this compiled-in, injected by `peios.login=1`. It does",
    "not any more — registryd is the only service peinit still defines itself,",
    "because it is the only one whose definition cannot live in the registry it",
    "serves. Everything else, the authority included, is registry data.",
    "",
    "Readiness is Notify (0), and it is load-bearing rather than a formality:",
    "authd signals READY=1 once /run/logon.sock is bound. lpsd requires authd,",
    "so without a real readiness signal lpsd would race the authority to the",
    "socket and fail its first connect on a cold boot. 'The process exists' is",
    "not the same statement as 'the socket is accepting'.",
    "",
    "ErrorControl is Critical (1). A boot that was asked for the login path and",
    "cannot start the authority has not done what it was asked, and should say",
    "so loudly rather than present a prompt that can never be satisfied. The",
    "consequence is real -- a failure aborts the boot, reboots, and lands in",
    "Recovery once the attempt counter trips -- and the escape hatch is",
    "`peios.recovery=1` on the kernel command line, which reaches a shell",
    "without starting any of this.",
    "",
    "No RuntimeDirectories: authd's three sockets (logon, ident, psi) all sit",
    "directly in /run, which peinit mounts in Phase 1. lpsd needs one; authd",
    "does not.",
    "",
    "No Requires. The authority depends on nothing -- sources dial in to it,",
    "which is why the edge lives on lpsd and points here rather than the other",
    "way round.",
    "",
    "Provides names the authn role, and that is what orders every service with",
    "a non-SYSTEM Identity after this one. peinit cannot start such a service",
    "without a token, and cannot get a token before /run/logon.sock is bound,",
    "so the dependency is real; before PEI-601 it was written down nowhere and",
    "all three LocalService definitions in the tree raced this socket. peinit",
    "synthesises the edge from Identity and resolves it through this key, so",
    "no service names authd directly and an image may ship another authority.",
    "",
    "Shipped by the authd package into /usr/share/regim/; inert until an image",
    "names it in [registry] autoapply."
  ],
  "keys": [
    { "path": "Machine\\System" },
    { "path": "Machine\\System\\Services" },
    {
      "path": "Machine\\System\\Services\\authd",
      "values": [
        { "name": "ImagePath",     "type": "sz",    "data": "/sbin/authd" },
        { "name": "Triggers",      "type": "multi", "data": ["boot"] },
        { "name": "Identity",      "type": "sz",    "data": "SYSTEM" },
        { "name": "Provides",      "type": "multi", "data": ["authn"] },
        { "name": "Readiness",     "type": "dword", "data": 0 },
        { "name": "RestartPolicy", "type": "dword", "data": 1 },
        { "name": "ErrorControl",  "type": "dword", "data": 1 },
        { "name": "DisplayName",   "type": "sz",    "data": "Authentication authority" },
        { "name": "Description",   "type": "sz",    "data": "PGSS Logon authority: mints KACS tokens and logon sessions" }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
